            <div xml:id="d628">

                <pb facs="0714" n="621" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg621"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">814.00/1199: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-05-02T12:00:00-06:00">May 2, 1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received
                        2:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>17. Department’s telegram No. 11, April 30, 6 p.m. The Department’s view of my
                    conversations is correct. I have no valid reason to think that the second
                    impression mentioned in the last paragraph of the telegram exists in Government
                    circles here. I would like therefore, before taking any steps in the sense
                    indicated by the Department, to obtain the Department’s views on one or two
                    specific points which I will submit by next air mail.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
